d}\nF(r(t)) \\cdot r^{′}(t) &= (t^{5}i - t^{6}j) \\cdot (3t^{2}i + 2tj) \\\\\n&= 3t^{7} - 2t^{7} \\\\\n&= t^{7}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_(C)F(r) \\cdot dr &= ∫_{0}^{1}F(r(t)) \\cdot r^{′}(t)dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}t^{7}dt\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133566 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r$ given that $\\mathbf F(x, y) = y \\,\\mathbf i + (x+y)\\,\\mathbf j$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t) = (1+2t)\\,\\mathbf{i} + (1-t)\\,\\mathbf{j}$ for $t \\in [0, 1]$."] [17592186133566 :question/worked-solution "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\int\\limits_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = \\int_a^b\\mathbf F(\\mathbf r (t))\\cdot \\mathbf r'(t)\\,\\textrm d t\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C$, we have\n\n$$\nx = 1 + 2t, \\qquad y = 1 - t\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(t)) &= yi + (x + y)j \\\\\n&= (1 - t)i + ((1 + 2t) + (1 - t))j \\\\\n&= (1 - t)i + (t + 2)j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr^{′}(t) &= \\frac{dx}{dt}i + \\frac{dy}{dt}j \\\\\n&= \\frac{d}{dt}(1 + 2t)i + \\frac{d}{dt}(1 - t)j \\\\\n&= 2i - j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF(r(t)) \\cdot r^{′}(t) &= ((1 - t)i + (t + 2)j) \\cdot (2i - j) \\\\\n&= (1 - t) \\cdot 2 + (t + 2) \\cdot (-1) \\\\\n&= 2 - 2t - t - 2 \\\\\n&=-3t\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can evaluate the integral, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∫_(C)F(r) \\cdot dr &= ∫_{0}^{1}f(r(t)) \\cdot r^{′}(t)dt \\\\\n&= ∫_{0}^{1}(-3t)dt \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}t^{2} \\mid _{0}^{1} \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2} - 0 \\\\\n&=-\\frac{3}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186133633 :question/problem "Evaluate $\\displaystyle\\int\\limits_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r$ given that $\\mathbf F(x, y, z) = x \\,\\mathbf i + y\\,\\mathbf j + z\\,\\mathbf k$ and $C$ is the path $\\mathbf r(t) = {t}\\,\\mathbf{i} + t^2\\,\\mathbf{j} + t^3\\